#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:30
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:32
msgid "Set up a document library in a few minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:34
msgid "What Document Engine does"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:35
msgid "Document Engine turns WordPress into a document library. Each file (PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, images, audio, video, archives) becomes a <strong>document</strong> with its own title, description, categories, tags and page. You publish documents in searchable libraries, show PDFs in a built-in viewer, and let visitors download them through one file server that counts downloads and applies access rules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:36
msgid "It also includes Post to PDF: a \"Download PDF\" button that turns posts and pages into PDFs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:38
msgid "<strong>Free</strong>: documents, libraries (table, grid, folders) with instant search and filters, the PDF viewer, preview popups, lists, search box, QR codes, Post to PDF, format requests, migration from other plugins, Elementor widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:39
msgid "<strong>Pro</strong>: access control and private files, share links, secure viewer, email gate, activity and reading analytics, versions, review and expiry dates, read-and-confirm, notifications, import, custom fields, client portal, handbook PDFs, AI assistant, abuse protection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:42
msgid "Install and activate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:44
msgid "In Plugins → Add New, search for \"Document Engine\", then install and activate it. Or upload the ZIP under Plugins → Add New → Upload Plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:45
msgid "A <strong>Documents</strong> menu appears in the admin sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:46
msgid "Requirements: WordPress 6.6 or newer and PHP 7.4 or newer. Post to PDF needs the PHP mbstring and gd extensions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:48
msgid "Pro is a separate add-on plugin that needs the free plugin. See \"Install Pro\" in the Pro features section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:50
msgid "Recommended first setup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:52
msgid "Open Documents → Settings → Documents. Keep <strong>Pages</strong> on so every document has its own page, and choose what the <strong>Download button</strong> does (download or open in the browser)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:53
msgid "Under Documents → Settings → Documents → Library, pick the default layout and documents per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:54
msgid "Create a few categories under Documents → Categories (for example Policies, Minutes, Forms)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:55
msgid "Under Documents → Settings → Advanced → Permissions, choose which roles manage all documents and which can publish their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:56
msgid "Add your first documents, then publish a library page (next articles)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:58
msgid "Open settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:60
msgid "Add your first document"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:62
msgid "Go to Documents → Add New Document."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:63
msgid "Enter a title. In the sidebar's <strong>Document file</strong> panel, upload a file, pick one from the Media Library, or link to a file on another site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:64
msgid "Optionally write a description in the editor, and choose categories and tags."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:65
msgid "Publish. The document gets a page (for example <code>/documents/annual-report/</code>) with a download button and, for PDFs, the viewer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:67
msgid "To turn many existing Media Library files into documents at once, select them in Media → Library (list view) and use the \"Create documents\" bulk action. With Pro you can also import a CSV file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:72
msgid "Create a page, for example \"Documents\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:73
msgid "Add the <strong>Document Library</strong> block. In the block sidebar choose the layout (table, grid or folders), columns, which categories to include, and which filters visitors see."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:74
msgid "Publish. Visitors can search instantly, filter, sort and page through the documents. The address updates as they filter, so filtered views can be shared."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:76
msgid "Not using the block editor? Use the shortcode <code>[document_engine_library]</code> (see Developers → Shortcodes) or the Elementor \"Document Library\" widget."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:82
msgid "Free features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:84
msgid "Everything included in the free plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:86
msgid "Documents and document pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:87
msgid "Documents are a post type with categories and tags. Each has a file (uploaded, from the Media Library, or an external link), a download counter and, when <strong>Pages</strong> is on, its own page showing the file type, size, last update, categories, a download button and, for PDFs, the viewer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:89
msgid "<strong>Where</strong>: Documents → All Documents and Add New Document."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:90
msgid "<strong>Download or open</strong>: the site default is set in Settings → Documents → Download button; each document can override it in the Document file panel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:91
msgid "<strong>File links</strong> go through <code>/?dengine_download=ID</code>, so counts and (with Pro) access rules always apply. Replacing a file keeps the same link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:92
msgid "<strong>Site search</strong> includes documents unless you switch it off in Settings → Documents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:93
msgid "The documents list shows the file, category, downloads and last update, with filters for category and file type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:95
msgid "Limitation: the free plugin does not restrict who can download a published document. Anyone with the link can download it. Use Pro access control for private documents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:97
msgid "Document Library: search, filters and layouts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:98
msgid "The Document Library block (and shortcode, and Elementor widget) lists documents as a table, a grid of cards, or folders by category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:100
msgid "<strong>Search</strong> updates results as visitors type, and also works without JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:101
msgid "<strong>Filters</strong>: category (with document counts), tag, file type, year, author and sort order. Turn on <strong>Let visitors pick several</strong> to replace the category, tag and file type dropdowns with checkboxes so visitors can combine choices. Picks within one filter widen the results; different filters narrow them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:102
msgid "<strong>Active filters</strong> show as removable chips above the results, with \"Clear all\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:103
msgid "<strong>Shareable</strong>: the page address carries the search and filters (for example <code>?dl_cat=policies,forms</code>)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:104
msgid "<strong>Columns</strong> (table) or card details (grid): thumbnail, title, description, category, tags, type, size, date, updated, author, downloads, download button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:105
msgid "Several libraries on one page each keep their own search and filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:107
msgid "Folder view lists each category as a folder. When a visitor searches or filters, it switches to a flat result list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:109
msgid "PDF viewer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:110
msgid "A built-in viewer based on PDF.js, served from your own site (no third-party viewer). It is used on document pages, in the PDF Viewer block and <code>[document_engine_viewer]</code>, and in preview popups."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:112
msgid "Page navigation, zoom (fit width, fit page, percentages), print, download, full screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:113
msgid "Search inside the PDF (Ctrl/Cmd+F while the viewer has focus) with highlighted matches."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:114
msgid "A sidebar with page thumbnails and the PDF's outline (bookmarks)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:115
msgid "Clickable links inside PDFs, including links to other pages of the same PDF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:116
msgid "Deep links: add <code>#page=5</code> to a document page address to open the PDF at page 5."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:118
msgid "Defaults are in Settings → PDF Viewer. Each block can override height, zoom, starting page and the toolbar buttons."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:119
msgid "PDFs linked from another website only display if that site allows it (CORS). Upload the file, or use a document with an uploaded file, for reliable viewing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:121
msgid "Preview popup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:122
msgid "With Settings → Documents → Library → <strong>View opens</strong> set to \"A preview popup\", the View button in libraries opens the document in a popup instead of going to its page: PDFs in the viewer, images, audio and video natively. The popup has Open page and Download buttons and closes with Esc."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:123
msgid "The popup only shows documents the visitor may open. Other file types (Word, Excel…) have no View button."
msgstr ""

