msgid "Section"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:325
msgid "What it controls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:331
msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:333
msgid "Step-by-step answers to common tasks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:335
msgid "Publish a policy library with filters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:337
msgid "Create a \"Policies\" category and add your policies to it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:338
msgid "On a new page, add a Document Library block. Under Documents to include, choose the Policies category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:339
msgid "Under Search and filters tick Tag, Year and Sort order; turn on Let visitors pick several if visitors should combine tags."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:340
msgid "Add a Document Search block to your header (Appearance → Editor) pointing to this page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:343
msgid "Replace a file without breaking links"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:344
msgid "Open the document and use Replace in the Document file panel. The document keeps its page and download address, so links in emails and other pages keep working. With Pro, the previous file is kept in the version history."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:346
msgid "Link to a specific page of a PDF"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:347
msgid "Add <code>#page=</code> and the page number to the document page address, for example <code>/documents/annual-report/#page=12</code>. In a PDF Viewer block, set the starting page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:349
msgid "Make documents members-only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:351
msgid "Edit the category (or document) and set \"Who can open these documents\" to logged-in users or chosen roles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:352
msgid "Leave \"Protect files automatically\" on so the files move to private storage."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:353
msgid "Check Tools → Site Health: the Document Engine protection test must pass. On nginx, add the rule it shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:356
msgid "Share a document with someone outside your site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:357
msgid "Open the document, go to Access & security → Share link, type the recipient's name, tick \"Email me when it is first opened\", and create the link. Send it; it expires after the set number of days. Revoke it from the same panel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:359
msgid "Make staff confirm they read a policy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:361
msgid "Open the policy, go to Read & confirm, switch it on, choose the roles and a deadline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:362
msgid "Add a Required Reading block to your staff page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:363
msgid "Follow progress in Reports → Acknowledgements, send reminders, and export the evidence CSV."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:366
msgid "Build a register with reference numbers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:368
msgid "In Settings → Fields add \"Reference\" (text, Column and Sort) and \"Department\" (choice list, Column and Filter)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:369
msgid "Fill them in the Details panel, or import a CSV with cf:reference and cf:department columns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:370
msgid "In a Document Library block, tick the Reference and Department columns and the Department filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:373
msgid "Move from Download Monitor, WPDM or Barn2"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:375
msgid "Keep the old plugin active. Open Migrate, pick the source and run the preview."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:376
msgid "Run the migration. Check a few documents and pages that used the old shortcodes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:377
msgid "Deactivate the old plugin. Its shortcodes and download links keep working through Document Engine."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:384
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:386
msgid "Common problems and how to fix them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:388
msgid "Document pages show \"Page not found\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:389
msgid "Go to Settings → Permalinks and click Save (this refreshes the site's addresses). Also check that another page or post type does not use the same address as the URL prefix in Settings → Documents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:391
msgid "Someone cannot see the Documents menu or a screen"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:392
msgid "Check their role in Settings → Advanced → Permissions. Reports and Tools only appear for roles allowed to use them; Settings needs an administrator. Related screens are grouped: Categories holds Tags, Reports holds Activity, Searches, Leads, Acknowledgements and Format requests, Tools holds Import, Migrate and Handbook PDF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:394
msgid "The PDF viewer is blank or shows an error"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:396
msgid "External PDFs: the other site must allow cross-site loading (CORS). Upload the file instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:397
msgid "Mixed content: a site on https cannot load a PDF from http."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:398
msgid "Security or caching plugins that combine or delay JavaScript can break the viewer; exclude the Document Engine viewer script."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:401
msgid "Download counts do not go up"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:402
msgid "Downloads are counted when the file is requested through the document link. Check that Download counter is on, and that links point to the document (not directly to the file in /wp-content/uploads/). Requests from known bots are not counted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:404
msgid "Post to PDF fails or looks wrong"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:406
msgid "Blank or error: raise PHP's memory limit (256 MB recommended) and check that the mbstring and gd extensions are installed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:407
msgid "\"Too many PDF requests\": the per-visitor limit in Settings → Advanced was reached; wait a minute or raise the limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:408
msgid "Styling: try \"Theme styles\" off and add custom CSS in Settings → Post to PDF → Style."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:411
msgid "Emails do not arrive"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:412
msgid "Format requests, reminders and notifications use WordPress's email. If other WordPress emails (like password resets) also fail, install an SMTP plugin to send through a real mail service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:414
msgid "Site Health says protected files can be downloaded directly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:415
msgid "Your web server ignores .htaccess files (common on nginx). Add the rule shown in the Site Health test to the site's nginx configuration and reload nginx, or ask your host. Until then, anyone who learns a protected file's exact address could download it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:418
msgid "Members see the wrong list, or a page cache shows private content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:419
msgid "Pages with personal lists (My Documents, Required Reading) tell caching plugins not to cache them. For library pages that show restricted documents differently to members, exclude logged-in users from your page cache (most caching plugins do this by default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:421
msgid "Search does not find words inside a file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:422
msgid "File text is indexed in the background after upload; large files can take a minute. Run <code>wp dengine reindex</code> to rebuild it. Scanned PDFs (images of text) contain no text to index."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:424
msgid "Pro licence or updates do not work"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:425
msgid "Check the key in Settings → License (it shows the status and renewal date). If it says the key \"has reached its site limit\", deactivate it on another site or upgrade the licence. Your server must be able to reach the store over https. Pro keeps working without an active licence; only updates need one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:431
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:433
msgid "Short answers to frequent questions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:435
msgid "Is the free version limited in time or in number of documents?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:436
msgid "No. The free plugin has no time limit and no document limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:438
msgid "Does it work with my theme and page builder?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:439
msgid "Libraries use your theme's fonts and colors and adapt to the space they get. Blocks work in the block editor and site editor; Elementor has its own widgets; shortcodes work anywhere else. Templates can be overridden in your theme (see Developers)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:441
msgid "Will my version 1 shortcodes and blocks keep working?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:442
msgid "Yes. Version 1 shortcodes, the PDF block, settings and the settings page address are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:444
msgid "Can I keep documents private with the free plugin?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:445
msgid "You can keep documents as drafts or private posts (only editors see them), but a published document can be downloaded by anyone who has the link. Member-only access, private file storage and share links are Pro features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:447
msgid "What happens when I uninstall?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:448
msgid "By default nothing is deleted, so you can reinstall without losing documents. To remove everything, turn on Settings → Advanced → When deleting the plugin before deleting it. Uploaded files in the Media Library are never deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:450
msgid "What happens if my Pro licence expires?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:451
msgid "Pro keeps working; you stop receiving updates and support until you renew."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:453
msgid "Does it support multisite?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:454
msgid "The plugin works per site: activate it on each site that needs it; every site keeps its own documents and settings."
msgstr ""

